=== D. ANTI-STUB AUDIT RATINGS ===

tools/benchmark.py — REAL.
  Imports engine.game (BIG_BLIND, STARTING_STACK) and sandbox.match.run_match
  at module load. Calls run_match() for every target (lines 332, 386).
  Supports --bot artifact-bound mode, --all-templates, --ablate-overlay,
  --self-play --vs-prior. ~24 KB, 346 LOC of net changes vs scaffold.

tools/self_play.py — REAL.
  Builds source-shim or zip mount; loops batches of run_match with deterministic
  per-batch seed (seed + batch * 1000003). Reports chip_delta and bot_errors.

tools/exploit_check.py — PARTIAL (documented).
  Loads the artifact zip and invokes its decide() on 20 fixed public states.
  Module docstring explicitly states: "This is not a Nash exploitability
  proof... assigns a local counterplay-risk score from the returned action."
  Score is derived from the bot's actual decisions, not a hardcoded table.
  Less rigorous than the Claude variant (no best_response - call EV calc),
  but not a stub.

tools/package.py — REAL.
  Same as scaffold; build() writes shim bot.py + src/ + data/ into zip with
  --strict re-open check.

tools/import_audit.py — REAL.
  Unchanged from scaffold.

src/bot.py — REAL.
  Imports OpponentModel, _preflop_lookup, _decide_postflop, canonical_hand,
  hand_score, sizing_to_amount, run_with_budget. Real decide() path.
  Retains POKERBOT_DISABLE_OVERLAY env var. Last commit "X1 patch: remove
  opponent-identity branching from src/bot.py" — verified in diff that
  archetype-by-name branching was removed in favor of behavior-based.

Verdict: All tools are REAL or documented PARTIAL. No evidence of fake
verification.

Codex's exploit_check.py is the weaker of the two (heuristic score vs.
Claude's EV-difference calc). Codex's reported preflop=18.0 / aggregate=7.4
mbb/g is not directly comparable to Claude's preflop=32.1 / aggregate=91.2
because the scoring functions differ.

